From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:17:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 161/174] tune: fine control on every draggable control of the
 CineCam Grade panel

The panel's controls were all absolute: the wheel puck jumped to the click and
one pixel was one pixel of full amplitude, a QSlider handle followed the mouse
so a whole range lived in 200 px of groove, and the CDL and channel fields could
not be dragged at all. Nothing on the panel could be nudged.

Everything draggable is now relative, with one convention across the panel:
a press never moves the value, a drag adds mouse delta x step, and one step is
one pixel, one wheel notch and one arrow key. Shift is ten times finer while
held (read on every mouse move, so switching mid-drag changes the speed and
never jumps the value), Ctrl ten times coarser. Typing a number stays exact.

Conventions copied rather than invented: relative trackball drag from Resolve's
and Baselight's wheels and from CRYENGINE's own PropertyRowNumberField::
onMouseDrag; drag-to-scrub numeric fields from Resolve, Nuke and Lightroom;
Shift-fine / Ctrl-coarse from Resolve, Photoshop and QAbstractSpinBox (the
legacy property tree has those two the other way round, which is why the header
says why we do not follow it there).

- CCineScrubSlider replaces QSlider: the press only opens the gesture (no
  teleport, no page step toward the click), a drag scrubs, wheel and arrows
  step, double-click and right-click ask for neutral. The 0..1000 groove is only
  a picture now; the owner keeps the float, so a Shift-fine scrub finer than one
  groove position is still a real edit.
- CCineScrubSpinBox replaces QDoubleSpinBox: it filters its own line edit so a
  drag past 3 px scrubs while a shorter press still places the caret, keeps a
  full-precision running value during the scrub, and emits the panel's three
  gesture signals instead of valueChanged - one undo step per scrub.
- CCineWheelDisc: SetFromPos (absolute) -> MovePuck (relative), with the gain
  per disc diameter so the feel is the same at every dock width; a wheel notch
  pushes the puck out or in along its direction, and is ignored when the wheel
  is neutral so the panel still scrolls.

The step sizes live in one place, namespace Step at the top of
CineGradeWidgets.h, chosen from what a step does to the picture: Lift channels
0.001, Gamma/Gain channels 0.005, masters 0.002/0.005, Contrast 0.005, Pivot
0.002, Saturation 0.005, curve stops 0.01, sat curve 0.005, CDL slope/offset/
power 0.005/0.001/0.005, and a wheel drag gain of 0.28 of the disc per diameter
of mouse travel. A slider's whole range needs about 800 px of sweep.

Undo, the IGradeEditTarget write path, the live viewport update and the dock
resize behaviour are untouched.

